# Bad default value for "Product::pack_stock_type" - Inheritance issue when loading Pack class (that inherit Product)

The default value of Product::pack_stock_type is set as "Pack::STOCK_TYPE_DEFAULT;" which in turn has a default value PackStockType::STOCK_TYPE_DEFAULT.

This is an inheritance issue because Pack class inherit product so when a Pack class is instantiated before the class loader attempt to load the Product class. Before of all the class loader assign valued to class field and the value from Product::pack_stock_type is a field of Pack ... that is the class i attempt to instantiate at the beginning..

In normal situation this issue pass unnoticed because in class_index.php the class is loaded by alphabetic order but is pure luck.
In certain specific situation this may conduce to an error of "ClassNotFoundException".
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/9608268/178926510-92a88007-89bf-44f3-9577-f2c56f1c8e5e.png)

The solution is to load directly the default value as "Product::pack_stock_type = PackStockType::STOCK_TYPE_DEFAULT;".

in fact all the other fields of products ha similar default value ex:
public $out_of_stock = OutOfStockType::OUT_OF_STOCK_DEFAULT;
public $redirect_type = RedirectType::TYPE_NOT_FOUND;

## Attendu
the default value for
Product::pack_stock_type 
should be set directly as Product::pack_stock_type =PackStockType::STOCK_TYPE_DEFAULT;

## Étapes
1. create an override of the product class : so in /override/classes create a file named Product.php and paste the code in the attached file ([Product.txt](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/files/9109613/Product.txt)
 or so:
```
class Product extends ProductCore
{
    public static function initStatic()
    {
        $test = self::$definition['fields'];
    }

}

if (method_exists('Product', 'initStatic')) {
    Product::initStatic();
}
```

2. clear the cache of prestashop to enable the override (so that the prestashop remake the class index including the new override). this can be done emptying the var/cache folder or going to BO->Advanced parameters->performance than "clear cache".

3. go in a page of the backoffice ex BO->Advanced parameters->performance (if you are already in this page refresh the page). or BO->modules->modules management. You will get the error. if you enable the debug mode the error detail will be shown

